From: Ken Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 07:29:41 -0700
Subject: Reset base level to 0 during ASTC uploads on PowerVR.

Add a workaround which resets the base level of the texture to 0
during glCompressedTexSubImage2D uploads of ASTC data. Apply this
workaround on Imagination's drivers.

Also apply the workaround to ClearCompressedTextureLevel and
ClearCompressedTextureLevel3D, as the validating command decoder's
texture clearing path uses glCompressedTexSubImage2D internally to
initialize uncleared compressed textures, which would otherwise
trigger the same crash.

Co-authored with Gemini.

Test: out/AndroidRelease/bin/gl_tests --use-cmd-decoder=validating \
  --gtest_filter=*ASTCCompressedSubImageWithBaseLevel*
